  "articleBody": "When you're dealing with structural walls, even small mistakes can lead to big problems down the line. One frequent error is misaligned or out-of-plumb framing. This can mean your new wall isn't perfectly straight, leading to issues with drywall installation and a less than stellar finish. To avoid this, make sure everything is checked for plumb and level multiple times before fastening anything permanently. Another common pitfall is uneven framing surfaces, which can cause buckling or a wavy look once the finishes are applied. This often comes from not ensuring all studs are flush with each other. Improper panel or sheathing support is another big one; without adequate backing, your walls won't be as sturdy as they should be. And of course, jumping into a structural wall project without getting the necessary permits is a huge no-no. Structural framing is part of your home's core support, so local building codes definitely apply. Always get permits before you start any work. If you're feeling overwhelmed, or just want to ensure it's done right, bringing in experienced professionals like us at HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of headaches and costly fixes.",
